MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_001: Hooo... Hyeh! Yah! Hah!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_002: That was amazing! I've been fascinated by your\nskills since I first saw you in the games.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_003: I suppose they must seem unusual to anyone who's\nfrom outside my village.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_004: The techniques are uniquely refined martial arts that\nhave been practiced in my hometown for a long time.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_005: Whoa, really? Do you think you could teach me?
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_006: I'd be happy to. But why do you want to learn? You\nalready know how to fight.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_007: Well, I've learned how to fight from a bunch of\ndifferent people.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_008: Pop taught me first. But I've sparred with\nTheodora too.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_009: And Bertrand taught me how to use a sword. Even\nlocked up in prison, he was real strong.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_010: I see. So your skill comes from training under\ndifferent people.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_011: Well, then, let's start with the basics.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_012: Yes! Thank you, Anatolia!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_013: Alright, let's go! Yah! Hyah! Hyyyah!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_014: Not like that. Be more mindful of your center of\ngravity. You lose it every time you strike.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_015: Oh, uh, OK. So, like... HRRAAAH!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_016: You need to focus on your core. Without that, you\ncan't transmit your power properly.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_017: Haaah... Haaah... Well it doesn't take much strength,\nbut concentrating is hard.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_018: Maybe I'm pushing you too much... My intention was\nonly to teach you as clearly as possible.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_019: Nah, it's fine. I asked you to teach me. And it's fun\nlearning from you.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_020: You enjoy it? I can't say I experienced that feeling\nwhen I was training.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_021: We Mediators acquire these techniques as a matter\nof course.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_022: Yeah? So you're able to do those moves right from\nthe very start?
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_023: No, not at all. When Master Long was first teaching\nme, I barely understood what he was saying.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_024: I had moments where I felt like I'd never get it... And\nmy teacher would laugh and tell me not to rush it.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_025: Perhaps at those times he wasn't sure how best to\nteach me. I feel similarly right now, actually.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_026: I should have taken my time and considered how to\nteach you... I'm sorry to have let you down.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_027: Wha— No, no, you're overthinking things!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_B_028: I'm glad you taught me today. And I'll get the hang \nof it—don't you worry!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_001: Centering breath... Focus on sending strength from\nmy core to the outside...
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_002: Precisely. Be mindful of the flow. Use minimum\nenergy for maximum advantage here.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_003: Hoo... Hyah! Yah! HYAAH!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_004: You've made excellent progress, Cai. Your growth\nfrom when you first started is very clear.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_005: I had to slip into Cai-style, but it went OK. I've been\nfocusing on my breathing in my regular training.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_006: Once the concentration part of your training comes\nmore naturally to me, I'll be a lot better, I think.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_007: Oh, yeah? Hehe. Well, I like your strategy.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_008: What's so funny?
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_009: My experience was a lot like yours. Even when I was\neating or sleeping—I was always thinking of my core.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_010: Really? I'm approaching it the way you did?
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_011: Mhm. Perhaps Master Long experienced this as a\nteacher too.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_012: Knowing that what a student doesn't grasp at first\nwill come in time.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_013: When he had a good laugh, it was because he was\nlooking forward to that day.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_014: Cai, I have to thank you. Because of you, I feel like I\nunderstand Master Long better now.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_015: Hehe. Glad to hear it!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_016: Anyway, there's another thing I wanted to show you.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_017: Hooo... HRRRAAGH!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_018: I swing the spear, transferring power like you said.\nThen step into it, like Pop taught me.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_019: I see! So you've taken what you learned from me\nand incorporated it, creating something entirely new!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_020: Cai, would you be willing to teach me Castor's\nspear technique?
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_021: Of course! If you're OK with me being the teacher,\nI'll show you anything you want!
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_022: Hmm... What's the best way to pass along what Pop\ntaught me? Your style is so different from mine.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_023: Sounds like you're considering it as I did. I think\nMaster Long would have loved to see this.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_024: Sharing what we've learned with new students and\ngaining deeper insights. It's wonderful.
MID_SE_Kai_Anh_A_025: Yeah, we can get better and better, together.